.TH SONNETTE\-AGENT 1 2026-11-04 garnish "garnish manual"
.SH NAME
sonnette\-agent \- notification server that forwards a garnish guest's notifications to the host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sonnette\-agent
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sonnette\-agent
runs in the guest's user session. It is the guest's notification server: it
owns
.B org.freedesktop.Notifications
on the session bus and hands every notification to
.BR sonnette (1)
on the host over vsock port 8892. It only accepts connections from CID 2,
the host. Actions the user picks and notifications closed on the host come
back as the usual
.B ActionInvoked
and
.B NotificationClosed
signals.
.PP
It is started by
.B sonnette\-agent.service
in every user's session, and by D-Bus activation the first time an
application sends a notification.
.PP
The VM's name is the guest's hostname, which
.BR gerantd (1)
sets to the name of the VM's configuration. The sending application is the
.B desktop\-entry
hint it gave, or else the application
.BR carte\-agent (1)
started it as, found from the sender's
.BR app\-carte\-*.scope .
Icons given as files or icon names are looked up in the guest and sent as
PNG or SVG.
.PP
.B GetCapabilities
answers with what the host's server can do. Notifications sent while the
host isn't connected, such as during boot, wait in the agent (up to 32)
and are shown when it connects.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/sonnette\-agent.service
Starts the agent in every user's session.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus\-1/services/org.garnish.sonnette.service
Starts it on the first notification.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sonnette (1),
.BR carte\-agent (1),
.BR garnish (7)
